#HELPS

0 SUMMARY~

MOVEMENT                            GROUP
north south east west up down       follow group gtell split
northeast ne northwest nw
southeast se southwest sw
run exits recall
sleep wake rest stand

OBJECTS                             INFORMATION
get put drop give sacrifice         help credits commands areas socials
wear wield hold                     report score time weather where who
recite quaff zap brandish           color description password title
lock unlock open close pick         gainlist teachlist
inventory equipment look compare
eat drink fill
list buy sell value
move climb flip push pull turn

COMMUNICATION
gossip leveling music q/a
shout quiet info yell
say tell gtell reply
emote pose note channels

COMBAT                              OTHER
kill flee kick rescue disarm        ! save quit
dirt-kick backstab cast wimpy       practice train
bash

For more help, type 'help <topic>' for any command, skill, or spell.
Type 'help KEYWORD' to see a list of all of the available topics.
Also help on: DAMAGE DYING EXPERIENCE NEWS STORY TICK WIZLIST GUILDS
If you are new here, we recommend that you read BEGINNERS.

The COMMANDS topic shows only the commands that your current trust level
allows you to use.  Mortals and heroes will see only mortal commands here.
Immortal-only commands are documented under WIZHELP and will not appear to
non-immortals.
~

0 NE NORTHEAST NW NORTHWEST SE SOUTHEAST SW SOUTHWEST~
Syntax: <direction>

These are shorthand movement commands for the diagonal exits in a room.
Each direction functions the same way as typing the full diagonal, for
example "ne" moves northeast and "sw" moves southwest.  If the exit exists
and is open, you will step through it; otherwise you will be told the way
is closed or blocked.
~

0 ENTER RIDE MOUNT~
Syntax: enter
Syntax: ride <mount> / mount <mount>

ENTER uses a room's default portal or structure entrance when no explicit
exit keyword is given.  It is often used for doors, wagons, boats, or other
special entries that do not map cleanly to the six main directions.

RIDE and MOUNT allow you to climb onto a valid mountable creature or
vehicle.  While mounted you move with your mount and benefit from its speed;
use DISMOUNT to climb off.  Some areas restrict mounted travel.
~

0 CASTLE~
Syntax: castle
Syntax: castle <message>

Castle chat is the private channel for members of your castle.  Typing
castle with no arguments toggles whether you hear castle chat.  Supplying a
message sends it to every logged-in member of your castle.  Synonyms: CC and
"-".
~

0 IGNORE~
Syntax: ignore <name>
        ignore none
        ignore list

Adds or removes players from a personal ignore list.  Characters on your
ignore list cannot contact you via tells or channels.  The LIST option shows
who you are currently ignoring; NONE clears the entire list.
~

0 LISTEN~
Syntax: listen

Listen provides a short ambient description of the sounds around you in your
current room.  It is helpful for spotting nearby activity without moving.
~

0 REPAIR~
Syntax: repair <object>

Requests repairs from an NPC repair vendor on worn equipment.  The shopkeeper
will quote and charge a gold cost based on condition and item type before
restoring durability.  If the item cannot be repaired, you will be told why.
~

0 SECONDARY~
Syntax: secondary <weapon>

Equips the specified weapon in your off-hand if you have trained the
SECONDARY weapon skill.  This toggles dual wielding; to return to a single
weapon, wield your main-hand weapon normally.
~

0 TELEKINESIS TK CLAIRVOYANCE DANGER PROJECT SHIFT~
Syntax: telekinesis <target>
Syntax: tk <target>
Syntax: clairvoyance
Syntax: danger
Syntax: project <direction>
Syntax: shift <player>

Psionic utility commands:
- TELEKINESIS/TK attempts to move or lift a target with mental force.  It
  requires psionic training and enough mana to succeed.
- CLAIRVOYANCE briefly lets you scry your surroundings for concealed exits or
  threats without moving.
- DANGER (Danger Sense) gives you a quick pulse of awareness about nearby
  threats, warning you if a room or foe is particularly perilous.
- PROJECT sends your spirit one room at a time in the chosen direction,
  letting you scout ahead while your body stays behind.  Running out of
  control or mana will snap you back to your body.
- SHIFT teleports you directly to another player if the destination and your
  current room permit travel; many safe or special rooms block shifting.
~

0 CHANGES MOTD NEWS RULES STORY WIZLIST~
Syntax: changes
Syntax: motd
Syntax: news
Syntax: rules
Syntax: story
 Syntax: wizlist
 
 Information commands:
 - CHANGES lists recent game updates.
 - MOTD shows the message of the day you see on login.
 - NEWS lists recent news posts.
 - RULES displays the game rules and policies.
 - STORY recounts the world background.
 - WIZLIST shows the immortals of the realm in order of seniority.
 ~

0 LORE~
Syntax: lore <object>

Analyzes an object to reveal its type, magical properties, level, and any
special effects.  Higher lore skill gives more detailed information and a
better chance to identify cursed or hidden attributes.
~

0 AFK DAMAGENUMBERS~
Syntax: afk
Syntax: damagenumbers

AFK toggles an "away from keyboard" flag and message so others know you are
currently unavailable.  You will not auto-reply to tells while AFK.

DAMAGENUMBERS toggles numerical combat feedback on or off.  When enabled,
you will see the exact damage value in brackets after each hit you deliver
or receive, e.g. "Your slash devastates the orc! [-47]".  Bystanders in
the room always see the descriptive message without numbers regardless of
your setting.  The flag is saved across logins.
~

0 CRAWL JUMP~
Syntax: crawl
Syntax: jump

CRAWL lets you move through low passages or stay low to the ground to reduce
your profile; movement is slower while crawling.  JUMP clears pits, low
barriers, and similar hazards when the room allows it, sometimes avoiding
traps or terrain penalties.
~

0 DELET DELETE~
Syntax: delet
Syntax: delete

DELET is a safety guard that prepares you for character deletion.  Typing
DELETE after using DELET fully confirms removal of your character file.  Use
with caution; deleted characters cannot be recovered without immortal aid.
~

0 PROMPT~
Syntax: prompt
Syntax: prompt <format string>
Syntax: prompt all

Customizes the prompt shown at the bottom of your screen.  PROMPT with no
arguments shows your current setting; PROMPT ALL sets a detailed default.
Placeholders such as %h for hit points, %m for mana, %v for movement, %g for
gold, and %r for room name may be used to build your own display.
~

0 QUESTION~
Syntax: question
Syntax: question <message>

Toggles or uses the Q/A channel.  With no message, the command toggles your
subscription to the Q/A channel.  With a message, it broadcasts your question
to everyone listening on that channel so other players can help.
~

0 BANK BALANCE DEPOSIT WITHDRAW CONVERT~
Syntax: balance
Syntax: deposit <amount> [platinum|gold|silver|copper]
Syntax: withdraw <amount> [platinum|gold|silver|copper]
Syntax: convert

Banking commands let you store wealth safely.  All four commands require you
to be inside a bank room (look for the flag or ask a banker).

  BALANCE   -- Shows your current account balance in all denominations.

  DEPOSIT   -- Moves coins from your inventory into your bank account.
               Specify an amount and an optional coin type.  Examples:
                 deposit 100 gold
                 deposit 500 platinum
               If no coin type is given, gold is assumed.

  WITHDRAW  -- Retrieves coins from your bank account into your inventory.
               Same syntax as deposit.  You must have room in your inventory
               to carry the coins.

  CONVERT   -- Exchanges all your carried coins upward to the highest
               denomination possible (copper -> silver -> gold -> platinum).
               Handy before depositing to keep your inventory tidy.

Notes:
  - The bank earns 1% interest per real day on your balance.  Interest is
    applied automatically while you are logged in (once every 24 real hours,
    catching up to 7 days if you were offline).  Accounts below 1 platinum
    do not earn interest.
  - No fees are charged on deposits or withdrawals.
  - Pkiller characters cannot access banking services.
  - Your bank balance is retained across deaths and remorts.
~

0 BREW CONCOCT SCRIBE SHOOT PICK JUNK~
Syntax: brew <potion recipe>
Syntax: concoct <component list>
Syntax: scribe <scroll recipe>
Syntax: shoot <target>
Syntax: pick <direction/lock>
Syntax: junk <object>

Crafting and utility commands:
- BREW/CONCOCT create magical potions from components you carry.
- SCRIBE copies a spell into a blank scroll if you know the spell and have a
  quill.
- SHOOT uses a loaded projectile weapon to fire at your current target.
- PICK attempts to pick the lock on a door or container using your lockpicks
  and the PICK LOCK skill.
- JUNK destroys an unwanted object, clearing inventory space without leaving
  a corpse behind.
~

0 BACKSTAB BS BASH BERSERK BLINDING CONFUSE CRANE DOORBASH DIRT DISARM DISMOUNT ENERVATE FISTS HIT KICK MIND BLAST MINDBLAST MURDE MURDER NERVE NIGHTMARE RESCUE SMITE STUNNING TORMENT TRIP~
Syntax: backstab <victim>          Syntax: bs <victim>
Syntax: bash <victim>              Syntax: berserk
Syntax: blinding <victim>          Syntax: confuse <victim>
Syntax: crane                      Syntax: doorbash <door>
Syntax: dirt <victim>              Syntax: disarm
Syntax: dismount                   Syntax: fists
Syntax: hit <victim>
Syntax: kick <victim>              Syntax: murder <victim>
Syntax: mindblast <victim>
Syntax: nerve <victim>             Syntax: nightmare <victim>
Syntax: enervate <victim>          Syntax: rescue <ally>
Syntax: smite <victim>             Syntax: stunning <victim>
Syntax: torment <victim>           Syntax: trip <victim>

Advanced combat maneuvers.  Each of these abilities relies on its associated
skill or spell and often requires appropriate weapons or positioning.
- BACKSTAB/BS: attack from hiding for heavy opening damage with a piercing
  weapon.
- BASH: slam your foe to the ground, potentially stunning them.
- BERSERK: enter a battle frenzy to boost offense while losing some control.
- BLINDING/CONFUSE/ENERVATE/NIGHTMARE/SMITE/STUNNING/TORMENT: offensive
  techniques that inflict status effects; see the relevant skill for exact
  outcomes and save checks.
- CRANE and FISTS: unarmed fighting stances that improve hand-to-hand combat.
- DOORBASH: force a locked door open with brute strength instead of a key.
- DIRT: fling dirt to blind an opponent temporarily.
- DISARM: knock a weapon from your opponent's hand.
- DISMOUNT: climb off your current mount.
- HIT and MURDER/MURDE: direct physical attacks; HIT mirrors the normal KILL
  command while MURDER is always considered a hostile action.
- KICK, NERVE, TRIP: quick physical attacks aimed at disrupting foes.
- MINDBLAST: psionic assault that harms and can disorient foes if they fail
  their save.
- RESCUE: pull an ally out of melee by taking their opponent onto yourself.
~

0 AQUEST TOPTEN SEARCH TRACK HIDE LEVITATE SNEAK STEAL STEALTH STEEL SHOVE ROLL IRON MINDBAR PSIONIC PSYCHIC QUI QUIT~
Syntax: aquest
Syntax: topten
Syntax: search
Syntax: track <target>
Syntax: hide
Syntax: levitate
Syntax: sneak
Syntax: steal <object> <victim>
Syntax: stealth
Syntax: steel
Syntax: shove <victim>
Syntax: roll
Syntax: iron
Syntax: mindbar
Syntax: psionic
Syntax: psychic
Syntax: quit
Syntax: qui

Exploration and miscellaneous skills:
- AQUEST shows the status of the automatic quest system.
- TOPTEN displays the current leaderboard of notable characters.
- SEARCH actively looks for hidden doors, exits, or traps in the room.
- TRACK attempts to follow the trail of another character across rooms.
- HIDE, SNEAK, STEALTH, and STEEL are stealth toggles that help you move
  unseen or silently when trained.
- LEVITATE engages psionic lift, allowing you to float over some hazards.
- STEAL takes items from another character if you remain unnoticed.
- SHOVE pushes a target out of the current room into an adjacent one.
- ROLL and IRON are defensive stances that improve dodging or toughness.
- MINDBAR/PSIONIC/PSYCHIC toggle specialized psionic defenses or channels.
- QUIT (or QUI) cleanly saves your character and disconnects from the game
  when you are not in combat.
~

62 IMMORTAL~
This help topic covers miscellaneous immortal tools.  Type WIZHELP for a
complete listing of all immortal commands available to your trust level.
For staff communication see IMMTALK (:) and WIZINFO.  Immortal channels
and flags are logged; all actions with LOG_ALWAYS are permanently recorded.

See also: WIZHELP, PSTAT, WIZCHECK, FINGER
~

62 BEEP~
Syntax: beep <immortal>

BEEP sends a ping-style private message to the named immortal regardless of
whether they have the immortal channel muted.  Use it to get the attention
of an AFK immortal without broadcasting to the whole staff channel.

See also: IMMTALK, WIZINFO
~

62 TRANSFUSION~
Syntax: transfusion <target>

TRANSFUSION is a psionic skill that lets you sacrifice a portion of your
own hitpoints to restore a target's health.  The amount transferred
depends on your psionic skill level and constitution.  Cannot be used
if it would reduce you below a safe minimum HP threshold.

See also: PSIONICS, MINDBAR
~

0 ALIAS ALIASES~
Syntax:
alias <word> <command as a string>     (sets the alias)
alias delete <alias to delete>         (deletes an alias)
alias <word>                           (shows an alias)

e.g.: alias mm cast 'magic missile'
      alias delete mm

To see all the aliases you have, type alias and to see a specific alias
type: alias <alias name>.

There is a max of 20 aliases per character.
~

0 AREAS~
Syntax: areas

AREAS shows you a list of areas in the game.  Area names are shown with
recommended levels.  However, those recommendations are just a rough range
and it is a good idea to read road signs to determine if you are entering
somewhere that may be particularly dangerous.
~

0 ARRIVE DEPART~
Syntax: arrive <string>
        depart <string>

Sets the message that others see when you enter and leave rooms.

All messages must contain a $n where your name is to be placed and a
$t(or $T) where the direction is to be placed.

The difference between $t and $T is the directions that are defaulted.
$t (arrive/depart)= north, south, east, west, up, down
$T (arrive) = the north, the south, the east, the west, above, below
$T (depart) = the north, the south, the east, the west, up, down
~

0 AUTO AUTOLIST AUTOLOOT AUTOGOLD AUTOSAC AUTOEXIT AUTOASSIST AUTOSPLIT~
Syntax: autolist
        autoloot
        autogold
        autosac
        autoexit
        autosplit
        autoassist

ToC uses varies automatic actions, to ease the boredom of always splitting
gold and sacrificing corpses.  The actions are as follows:

autolist   : list all automatic actions
autogold   : take all gold from dead mobiles
autoloot   : take all equipment from dead mobiles
autosac    : sacrifice dead monsters (if autoloot is on, only empty corpses)
autoexit   : display room exits upon entering a room
autosplit  : split up spoils from combat among your group members
autoassist : makes you help group members in combat

Typing a command sets the action (except for autolist); typing it again removes
it.  When you create a new character, the default is for all of the automatic
actions to be on.

AUTO is equivalent to autolist and also shows the status of the PROMPT,
COMBINE ITEMS, NOFOLLOW, NOSUMMON, and NOLOOT flags..
~

0 BRANDISH QUAFF RECITE ZAP~
Syntax: brandish
Syntax: quaff    <potion>
Syntax: recite   <scroll> <target>
Syntax: zap      <target>
Syntax: zap

BRANDISH brandishes a magical staff.  QUAFF quaffs a magical potion (as opposed
to DRINK, which drinks mundane liquids).  RECITE recites a magical scroll; the
<target> is optional, depending on the nature of the scroll.  ZAP zaps a
magical wand at a target.  If the target is not specified, and you are fighting
someone, then that character is used for a target.

You must HOLD a wand or a staff before using BRANDISH or ZAP.

All of these commands use up their objects.  Potions and scrolls have a single
charge.  Wands and staves have multiple charges.  When a magical object has no
more charges, it will be consumed.

These commands may require an item skill to be successful, see the help entries
on the SCROLLS, STAVES, and WANDS skills for more information.  No skill is
required to quaff a potion.
~

5 TEACHLIST~
Syntax: teachlist

This will show you a list of guildmasters and what they can teach you for skills/
spells. Some spells/skills will require that you learn the group they are in.
So also check out the gainlist command.
~

5 GAINLIST~
Syntax: gainlist

This will show you a list of guildmasters and what they will allow you to gain
for skills/spells. For information on every group you can consult the help.
The command teachlist will show you where you can learn which spell. So also
check out the teachlist command.
~

70 DNS~
Syntax: dns

This command will turn DNS lookups on and off.  Remember that with DNS lookups
turned off, sitebans on name hosts will be ignored.

~

70 GRANTPSI~
Syntax: grantpsi <player> [now] [skill1,skill2,...]

GRANTPSI is a level 70 tool to guarantee a player receives psionics. Without
"now" it flags the target for a 100%% success at the level-based psionic check
and optionally locks in a comma-separated list of psionic skills to award when
the check fires (default behavior rolls normally). Using "now" grants psionics
immediately, sends the unlock messaging, and applies the chosen skills right
away. Valid picks include: psionic armor, psychic shield, mindbar, torment,
ego whip, enervate, mindblast, clairvoyance, astral walk, shift, project,
telekinesis, transfusion, nightmare, mind leech, and confuse.

~

67 FSAVE~
Syntax: fsave

This command will force all the players to save, but doesn't send them a message
when you do it.  This command is also invoked on reboots and shutdowns.

~

0 BRIEF~
Syntax: brief

If brief is on, you will see only short descriptions of rooms when you
enter them and when you type LOOK.  Typing brief once, turns brief on; typing
it again, turns it off, allowing you to see full descriptions.

The default is for brief to be off.
~

0 BUY LIST SELL VALUE~
Syntax: buy   <object>
Syntax: list
Syntax: sell  <object>
Syntax: value <object>

BUY buys an object from a shop keeper.
When multiple items of the same name are listed, type 'buy n.item', where n
is the position of the item in a list of that name.  So if there are two
swords, buy 2.sword will buy the second.

LIST lists the objects the shop keeper will sell you.
List <name> shows you only objects of that name.

SELL sells an object to a shop keeper.

VALUE asks the shop keeper how much he, she, or it will buy the item for.
~

0 CAST~
Syntax: cast <spell> <target>

Before you can cast a spell, you have to practice it.  The more you practice,
the higher chance you have of success when casting.  Casting spells costs mana.
The mana cost decreases as your level increases.

The <target> is optional.  Many spells which need targets will use an
appropriate default target, especially during combat.

If the spell name is more than one word, then you must quote the spell name.
Example: cast 'cure critic' frag.  Quoting is optional for single-word spells.
You can abbreviate the spell name.

When you cast an offensive spell, the victim usually gets a saving throw.
The effect of the spell is reduced or eliminated if the victim makes the
saving throw successfully.

See also the help sections for individual spells.
~

0 CLIMB~
Syntax: climb <object>

In order to get between certain rooms, you must CLIMB a rope, ladder or
other object.  Read room descriptions carefully to find the object you need
to climb.
~

0 OPEN CLOSE LOCK UNLOCK~
Syntax: open   <object|direction>
Syntax: close  <object|direction>
Syntax: lock   <object|direction>
Syntax: unlock <object|direction>

OPEN and CLOSE open and close an object or a door.

LOCK and UNLOCK lock and unlock a closed object or door.  You must have
the requisite key to LOCK or UNLOCK.

Those with the appropriate skill can PICK locks, enabling them to open
locked doors or objects without having the key.  See help on PICK for more
information.
~

0 COLOR~
Syntax:  color on/off/list/default
         color <color type> <color>

The COLOR command is used to toggle color on or off and to set colors for
the various channels.

Typing the word COLOR alone will toggle color on or off.

COLOR DEFAULT is used to load the default colors for the various
channels.  If you turn color on without having set defaults, you will not
see any colors as they will all be set to grey.

COLOR LIST shows a list of the available colors.

To set the color for an indivdual type of message, use
COLOR <TYPE OF MESSAGE> <# of color>
The color number can be obtained using COLOR LIST.
For example, to make all gossips appear in yellow, type:
COLOR gossips 7
~

0 COMBINE~
Syntax: combine

If combine is on, you will see like items in your inventory combined on
a single line.  The number of items of that type you have will be shown in
parentheses in front of the item.

For example, if, with combine off, you see:
a big pot pie
a big pot pie
a big pot pie

with combine on you would see:
(3) a big pot pie

If combine is on, typing combine again turns it off, showing you the long
inventory again.  The default is for combine to be on.
~

0 COMMANDS~
Syntax: commands

COMMANDS shows you all the commands in the game.
~

0 COMPACT~
Syntax: compact

When COMPACT mode is on, your actions and the game responses are shown to
you without spaces between the lines.  Typing compact once turns compact
mode on; typing it again, removes compact mode, showing blank spaces between
lines again.

The default is for compact to be off.
~

0 COMPARE~
Syntax: compare <object-1> <object-2>
Syntax: compare <object>

COMPARE compares two objects in your inventory.  If both objects are weapons,
it will report the one with the better average damage.  If both objects are
armor, it will report the one with the better armor class.

COMPARE with one argument compares an object in your inventory to the object
you are currently wearing or wielding of the same type.

COMPARE doesn't consider any special modifiers of the objects.  You may
wish to wear, wield or hold an item which compares as worse if it has
bonuses, such as additions to attributes.  These modifiers can be determined
by using the IDENTIFY spell or the LORE skill..
~

0 CONSIDER~
Syntax: consider <character>

CONSIDER tells you what your chances are of killing a character.
When you consider a character, you will see two lines of information.
The first line refers to the relative level of you and the character you
are considering; the second refers to the relative number of hit points
(based on max hp, not current hp).  Between these two you should have a
rough idea of whether or not it is worth attempting the fight.
~

0 COUNT~
The count command displays the number of people (that you can see) logged
into the mud.  It also displays the highest number observed that day, if
it is higher.
~

0 CREDITS~
Syntax: credits

This command shows the list of the original Diku Mud implementors.
~

0 DELETE~
Syntax: delete <password>

Use the delete command to erase unwanted characters, so the name will be
available for use.  This command must be typed along with your password to
delete a character, and you cannot be forced to delete. Deletion is permanent.
You will not be restored for deleting yourself.
~

0 DESCRIPTION DESC~
Syntax: description <string>
Syntax: description + <string>

Sets your long description to the given string.  If the description string
starts with a '+', the part after the '+' is appended to your current
description, so that you can make multi-line descriptions.
~

0 DONATE~
Syntax: donate <object>

If you have items in your inventory that you no longer need, you may
wish to donate them for the use of other adventurers.  The donate command
allows you to do this even if you are far away from the Temple of Devota.
The donated item will be placed randomly in one of the donation pits -
either in the Temple of Devota or in one of the guild halls in Dresden.
~

0 DRINK EAT FILL~
Syntax: drink <object>
Syntax: eat   <object>
Syntax: fill  <object>

When you are thirsty, DRINK something.

When you are hungry, EAT something.

FILL fills a drink container with water from a fountain or pool.
~

0 DROP GET GIVE PUT TAKE~
Syntax: drop <object>
Syntax: drop <amount> coins
Syntax: get  <object>
Syntax: get  <object> <container>
Syntax: give <object> <character>
Syntax: give <amount> coins <character>
Syntax: put  <object> <container>

DROP drops an object, or some coins, on the ground.

GET gets an object, either lying on the ground, or from a container, or even
from a corpse.  TAKE is a synonym for get.

GIVE gives an object, or some coins, to another character.

PUT puts an object into a container.

DROP, GET and PUT understand the object names 'ALL' for all objects and
'ALL.object' for all objects with the same name.
~

0 EMOTE , POSE SOCIAL SOCIALS~
Syntax: emote <action>
Syntax: , <action>
Syntax: pose

Socials are a large set of specialized commands that let you do such things
as smile, wave, etc. to yourself, others or nobody in particular.  For a
complete list of the available actions, type SOCIAL.

EMOTE is used to express emotions or actions.  A shortcut for emote is ,.
EMOTE allows you to perform actions that are not built in.

POSE is a variant of EMOTE.  POSE selects a pose at random.  The poses are
dependent on your class.

The following is a (not necessarily complete) list of the socials which
exist in ToC:
gack        kiss        eve         bounce      smile       dance
cackle      laugh       giggle      shake       puke        growl
scream      comfort     sigh        sulk        hug         snuggle
